{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "player",
  "category": "player",
  "status": "provisional",
  "comment": "THE PROTAGONIST, from the user's own character sheet (art/player/source/character-sheet.png, kept bit for bit; art/player/source/character-sheet.json says where each pose is and which clip it is): every frame is a pose of that sheet with the white background taken off, scaled once per clip so that the head is the same size in every animation, and placed by a translation — nothing is redrawn, recoloured or deformed. Each clip is handed over with `npm run assets:intake` and its sources are archived in art/player/source/delivered/<clip>/. The six clips the sheet has no drawing for (attack2, crouch, crouchWalk, aerialAttack, crouchAttack, drink) are DERIVED (tag `derived`): `npm run assets:derive` makes them from the owner's own drawings — the puppet warp, a few rigid moves of the whole figure and, for the drink, a vial and a small arm drawn over the owner's idle — following the recipes of tools/assets/heroDerivedClips.ts (docs/PROMPT24-LOG.md, F5); a drawing of the owner's, handed over with `npm run assets:intake -- <clip> --accept`, replaces a derived clip and is never made again. The design this replaced is kept, in the layout of art/player/, in art/player/archive/design-v1/ (and in git commit 48684b9, the last one that had it in the game).",
